within ;
package Modelica "Modelica Standard Library (subset adapted for this platform)"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Package;

  annotation (
    preferredView="info",
    version="4.0.0-subset",
    versionDate="2020-06-04",
    Documentation(info="<html>
<p>
The package <strong>Modelica&reg;</strong> is a <strong>standardized</strong> and <strong>free</strong> package
that is developed by the &quot;<strong>Modelica Association Project - Libraries</strong>&quot;.
It is also called <strong>Modelica Standard Library</strong>. It provides model components in many
domains that are based on standardized interface definitions.
</p>
<p>
This library is a <strong>subset</strong> of the Modelica Standard Library 4.0.0, adapted to the
Modelica subset supported by this platform (no arrays, functions, algorithms, redeclarations or
conditional components). The class tree, icons, parameter names, units and equations follow the
original library so that models built here look and behave like their MSL counterparts.
Contained sub-libraries:
</p>
<ul>
<li><a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Blocks\">Blocks</a> &ndash; input/output blocks (continuous, math, sources, nonlinear)</li>
<li><a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Electrical.Analog\">Electrical.Analog</a> &ndash; analog electrical components</li>
<li><a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational\">Mechanics.Rotational</a> &ndash; 1-dim. rotational mechanics</li>
<li><a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Mechanics.Translational\">Mechanics.Translational</a> &ndash; 1-dim. translational mechanics</li>
<li><a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Thermal.HeatTransfer\">Thermal.HeatTransfer</a> &ndash; lumped heat transfer</li>
<li><a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Units\">Units</a>, <a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Constants\">Constants</a>, <a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Icons\">Icons</a></li>
</ul>
<p>
<strong>Licensed by the Modelica Association under the 3-Clause BSD License</strong><br>
Copyright &copy; 1998-2020, Modelica Association and contributors.
</p>
<p>
<em>This Modelica package is <u>free</u> software and the use is completely at <u>your own risk</u>;
it can be redistributed and/or modified under the terms of the 3-Clause BSD license.
For license conditions (including the disclaimer of warranty) see LICENSE.md or visit
<a href=\"https://modelica.org/licenses/modelica-3-clause-bsd\">https://modelica.org/licenses/modelica-3-clause-bsd</a>.</em>
</p>
<p>
<strong>Modelica&reg;</strong> is a registered trademark of the Modelica Association.
</p>
</html>"));
end Modelica;
